All the reasonable properties you expect.
\begin{enumerate}
\item Composition of $\'\text{e}$tale is $\'\text{e}$tale.
\item $\'\text{E}$tale is closed under base change.
\item $X\xrightarrow{f}Y\xrightarrow{g}Z$ is $\'\text{e}$tale and $g$ is $\'\text{e}$tale means $f$ is $\'\text{e}$tale.
\end{enumerate}

The following properties are [[QNOU|fppf-local on the base]]:
\begin{enumerate}
\item surjective;
\item locally of finite type; locally of finite presentation;
\item of finite type; of finite presentation;
\item universally closed; universally open;
\item separate; proper; unramified; smooth; \'etale; affine; isomorphism; open immersion; closed immersion, ...
\end{enumerate}

If $\mathcal{C}$ is a site and $\mathrm{sh}(\mathcal{C})$ is the [[PDHD|category of sheaves]] on $\mathcal{C}$, then the forgetful functor $\mathrm{sh}(\mathcal{C})\to \hat{\mathcal{C}}$ has a left adjoint, i.e., for all $\mathcal{F}\in \widehat{\mathcal{C}}$, there is a unique $\mathcal{F}^a\in \mathrm{sh}(\mathcal{C})$ and an arrow $\mathcal{F}\to \mathcal{F}^a$ such that, for any $\mathcal{G}\in \mathrm{sh}(\mathcal{C})$,
		\[
			\begin{tikzcd}
				\mathcal{F}\ar[r] \ar[dr, swap, "\forall"] & \mathcal{F}^a\ar[d, dashed, "\exists !"]\\
				& \mathcal{G}
			\end{tikzcd}
		\]
